ht line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/85/85638c1466360f3e5285c34e84903824140b9e2fc72a0f029ab1ded170b64eb2.png)\n\n- $O,P,S$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/4b/4b7ef30e306e3c7e70dadb1524e1f60a9ea01832215009ef2ea8344cb07e7297.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186107321 :answer-field/correct 17592186107324 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-b615808c-9716-5264-afdc-7e0ca61bc6d9" :question/id #uuid "b615808c-9716-5264-afdc-7e0ca61bc6d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-13444" :question/problem "![](images/e9/e9ede3d8d40b90fcf4919b85917c2fa21bf91163d136a1cd40b8bd6c0db3b40d.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. Point $K$ is **not** collinear with the points $M$ and $N$\n\nII. Points $L,O,Q$ are collinear\n\nIII. Points $J,K,Q$ are **not** collinear" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is true. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/fa/fa3ac1e9323a72254ecfc2242b1de23c05f0cc639b593eeadacb64ed6b4d4036.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/88/8895800b4c1ca6d22d42fac0cdb1488f716bdb5b59b49496d2f908f0947314b0.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/f3/f39a0462a8a52762c7525e31746e69269ab4b9521f4cc4e8121b114e98ddb68a.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-570bf11a-a7c8-574f-b3ff-0a5d67734d64"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-570bf11a-a7c8-574f-b3ff-0a5d67734d64" :answer-field/id #uuid "570bf11a-a7c8-574f-b3ff-0a5d67734d64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio 