233ae5ef50df160ce12b1823725966d.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/da/da1fb5e45ddfc41a8a9ff592ade9e5f2d5411e07b8e6ed1cf4ddad7e5841f6ae.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/4f/4fd5a2ee4afd7c9d61b4d8e20cf676c602167d1d8f21a6392f36bcfeb54a8f25.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-90cfe79e-8e7f-59c5-abff-60f447c4b5f1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-90cfe79e-8e7f-59c5-abff-60f447c4b5f1" :answer-field/id #uuid "90cfe79e-8e7f-59c5-abff-60f447c4b5f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c6a6c0c2-54b4-5a92-ae43-3c73a889ccc7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cde9a6ef-ccf9-5ddd-90ad-26bc779618d0" "answer-26034fca-f6aa-5214-becb-da1b7bcfc8fa" "answer-c6a6c0c2-54b4-5a92-ae43-3c73a889ccc7" "answer-75fb88e8-ec3c-55a0-a798-82d2396679b1" "answer-745ffa8f-7fa1-51b7-8a78-b2549b96b19b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cde9a6ef-ccf9-5ddd-90ad-26bc779618d0" :answer/id #uuid "cde9a6ef-ccf9-5ddd-90ad-26bc779618d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26034fca-f6aa-5214-becb-da1b7bcfc8fa" :answer/id #uuid "26034fca-f6aa-5214-becb-da1b7bcfc8fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6a6c0c2-54b4-5a92-ae43-3c73a889ccc7" :answer/id #uuid "c6a6c0c2-54b4-5a92-ae43-3c73a889ccc7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75fb88e8-ec3c-55a0-a798-82d2396679b1" :answer/id #uuid "75fb88e8-ec3c-55a0-a798-82d2396679b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-745ffa8f-7fa1-51b7-8a78-b2549b96b19b" :answer/id #uuid "745ffa8f-7fa1-51b7-8a78-b2549b96b19b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-16cc09e7-7364-5574-b6ef-c0b00cd9e46e" :question/id #uuid "16cc09e7-7364-5574-b6ef-c0b00cd9e46e" :question/math-academy-id "q-155557" :question/problem "![](images/cb/cbf6838fbb72a7fcffbb621b813abbb5d1ccd0a517fcbba7878d4be3f64e8c11.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $M,$ $R,$ and $N$ are collinear\n\nII. $T,$ $S,$ and $P$ are collinear\n\nIII. $M,$ $R,$ and $S$ are **not** collinear" :question/worked-solution "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/bf/bf251981278e739aaefe7c62cfa8f50d4be39ffa079e358824aaeec2b1045469.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement II is false. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/af/aff25fea8765f1abf339eb406c1fe629699ede85a0afabd828e04c8a87449879.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/28/28e81082c0f342992b9123c88c39d288a53e9b30dc4f39ee048739349cd38425.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2d0b3959-8cb4-557d-9329-078083da0be4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2d0b3959-8cb4-557d-9329-078083da0be4" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d0b3959-8cb4-557d-9329-078083da0be4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9b9a4cab-649b-512f-805e-9c5bbe728cb0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9b9a4cab-649b-512f-805e-9c5bbe728cb0" "answer-0ad41565-a704-532b-bb33-f22b0b4d71bc" "answer-abf5e2cf-2b63-5eb9-a773-caf4bcbb7088" "answer-004b80fe-aa14-5965-b4ca-127d549ed72f" "answer-d83653ac-e94e-57a2-95af-ccfcad73a67c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b9a4cab-649b-512f-805e-9c5bbe728cb0" :answer/id #uuid "9b9a4cab-649b-512f-805e-9c5bbe728cb0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ad41565-a704-532b-bb33-f22b0b4d71bc" :answer/id #uuid "0ad41565-a704-532b-bb33-f22b0b4d71bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abf5e2cf-2b63-5eb9-a773-caf4bcbb7088" :answer/id #uuid "abf5e2cf-2b63-5eb9-a773-caf4bcbb7088" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-004b80fe-aa14-5965-b4ca-127d549ed72f" :answer/id #uuid "004b80fe-aa14-5965-b4ca-127d549ed72f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d83653ac-e94e-57a2-95af-ccfcad73a67c" :answer/id #uuid "d83653ac-e94e-57a2-95af-ccfcad73a67c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c2f5f2a-936e-5967-a391-3ffba6cfe5b2" :question/id #uuid "3c2f5f2a-936e-5967-a391-3ffba6cfe5b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-13447" :question/problem "![](images/50/50dfc42742418eae8eb25f26fd193b714e06b820f99945ac2b8b759eed3a349e.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $Q,S,T$\n\nII. $M,O,Q$\n\nIII. $N,P,T$" :question/worked-solution "- $Q,S,T$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/21/2101dd8ae066aa55d601263de389e013100e476ddbf5220381e4040440b344a9.png)\n\n- $M,O,Q$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/d2/d29ca68ff7123964944eded292ec8ea2c6b16a9fd46e875472e7666f114c8cad.png)\n\n- $N,P,T$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/03/03db0865e93c7c9a1a2f1c23fd8027602e04299903edb6996b9f0b2150d1d036.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9d2295c0-0388-59df-bc04-c7923000e5c6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9d2295c0-0388-59df-bc04-c7923000e5c6" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d2295c0-0388-59df-bc04-c7923000e5c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ad043a29-be6f-5876-9793-8872bb333157" :answer-field/choices ["answer-11c7107d-7a3f-5c78-b66e-f38c1897d9ec" "answer-d45dfc1c-3aef-5a5b-8f68-ad3953e1d907" "answer-ad043a29-be6f-5876-9793-8872bb333157" "answer-88c9cc9f-97f9-5a3a-ba24-2880c971b71a" "answer-339b3426-cf16-5642-a40a-711c00b84dee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11c7107d-7a3f-5c78-b66e-f38c1897d9ec" :answer/id #uuid "11c7107d-7a3f-5c78-b66e-f38c1897d9ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d45dfc1c-3aef-5a5b-8f68-ad3953e1d907" :answer/id #uuid "d45dfc1c-3aef-5a5b-8f68-ad3953e1d907" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad043a29-be6f-5876-9793-8872bb333157" :answer/id #uuid "ad043a29-be6f-5876-9793-8872bb333157" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88c9cc9f-97f9-5a3a-ba24-2880c971b71a" :answer/id #uuid "88c9cc9f-97f9-5a3a-ba24-2880c971b71a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-339b3426-cf16-5642-a40a-711c00b84dee" :answer/id #uuid "339b3426-cf16-5642-a40a-711c00b84dee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111906 :tutorial/content "For any two distinct points, there is always one (and only one) line that passes through them.\n\nFor example, the line passing through the points $P$ and $Q$ is $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{PQ},$ while the line that passes through $A$ and $B$ is $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{AB}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/8c/8c79a551e7ced71de157ea292baa3d7f38afaca4ea76ee467fc4add1b28ed33f.png)\n\nHowever, given three or more points, there is not always a line that passes through all of them.\n\nFor example, for the three points $F, G,$ and $H$ below, it is impossible to draw a single straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/30/30361c0bd49e571e317746f2d88848626da52e5ddbcda8fe9b6f496e4aff6b69.png)\n\nHowever, it is *sometimes* possible to draw a line through three (or more) points. In such cases, we say that the points are **collinear**.\n\nFor example, the points $M,$ $N,$ and $O$ shown below are collinear since they all lie on the same line.\n\n![](images/bf/bf3de55518c21de30718b2d9fee7032139c89aa3a4a963b8346b457ceafbeada.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110859 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
